      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Prompt and effective diagnosis and treatment for common shoulder problems depends on the ability of practitioners to distinguish between traumatic and non-traumatic shoulder conditions. This article aims to enable practitioners to make accurate assessments and carry out shoulder examinations, including the undertaking of selected special tests, before discharging or referring patients."},
